title: Angular Queuing Guide
id: queuing
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queuing stores operations in an ordered buffer and processes them individually. It is the primary Pacer strategy for work that should not be discarded when calls arrive faster than they can run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queues are lossless only while they have capacity. A finite "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"},{"type":"text","value":", explicit clearing, expiration, or a processing error can still remove or reject work."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-queuing-works","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How queuing works"}]},{"type":"code","value":"Queuing (process one item every 2 ticks)\nTimeline: [1 second per tick]\nCalls:        ⬇️  ⬇️  ⬇️     ⬇️  ⬇️     ⬇️  ⬇️  ⬇️\nQueue:       [ABC]   [BC]    [BCDE]    [DE]    [E]    []\nExecuted:     ✅     ✅       ✅        ✅      ✅     ✅\n             [======================================================]\n             ^ Accepted items remain queued until processed\n\n             [Items arrive]    [Process steadily]      [Empty]","lang":"text"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The queue can process automatically with a delay between items, or remain stopped for manual processing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-use-queuing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to use queuing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose queuing when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every accepted operation should run individually."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Processing order matters."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Incoming work may temporarily exceed processing capacity."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A maximum buffer size should reject excess work explicitly."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FIFO, LIFO, or priority ordering is required."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose another utility when:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only the final call matters. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./debouncing.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"debouncing"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Intermediate calls may be discarded while work runs steadily. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./throttling.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throttling"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calls should be rejected after a time-window quota. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./rate-limiting.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"rate limiting"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Items should run together. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./batching.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"batching"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tasks return Promises or should run concurrently. Use "},{"type":"link","href":"./async-queuing.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async queuing"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-an-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose an API"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuedSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuedValue"},{"type":"text","value":" for queue-driven signals"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuer"},{"type":"text","value":" for direct queue lifecycle and ordering control"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the queued state or value API when queue contents drive the UI. Use the instance API for ordering, capacity, expiration, pause, resume, flush, and manual processing."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"angular-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { injectQueuedSignal } from '@tanstack/angular-pacer'\n\nexport class JobQueueComponent {\n  readonly queued = injectQueuedSignal(processJob, { wait: 500 }, (state) => ({\n    items: state.items,\n    isRunning: state.isRunning,\n  }))\n\n  add() {\n    this.queued.addItem(nextJob())\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The focused snippets later in this guide use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuer"},{"type":"text","value":" and assume they run inside an Angular injection context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialItems"},{"type":"text","value":" when work is already available at creation time. The queue applies its normal insertion and capacity rules, and automatic processing can begin immediately unless "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"started: false"},{"type":"text","value":" is set."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"queue-a-source-signal","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queue a source signal"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuedValue"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueuedValueSignal"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued()"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the most recently processed value, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued.addItem(value)"},{"type":"text","value":" enqueues a value, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued.queuer"},{"type":"text","value":" exposes the queue controls. Its default selector exposes pending items at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued.queuer.state().items"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"readonly source = input.required<string>()\nreadonly queued = injectQueuedValue(this.source, { wait: 500 })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Construction does not read the source. Angular's effect reads it after inputs are bound and enqueues the latest value. Each later effect run enqueues the latest observed source value. Several source writes before an effect runs are coalesced; use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued.addItem"},{"type":"text","value":" for every value that must enter the queue individually."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Before processing begins, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued()"},{"type":"text","value":" reads the initial source value. Reading it before a required input is bound throws Angular's required-input error. Supply an explicit initial value if the output must be readable earlier:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const text = injectQueuedValue(source, '')\nconst object = injectQueuedValue(objectSource, { label: 'Loading' }, {})\nconst callback = injectQueuedValue(callbackSource, () => 'Loading', {})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two-argument primitive initial values, including "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"''"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":", are supported. Object and function initial values require a third options object, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":". A function in the options position is an options factory."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a fourth selector argument, which can be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":", when an explicit initial value uses factory or undefined options:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queued = injectQueuedValue(source, '', () => ({ wait: wait() }), undefined)\nconst initialObject = injectQueuedValue(objectSource, { label: 'Loading' }, undefined, undefined)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuedValue(source, options, undefined)"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the options-only meaning. An explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" initial value requires an options object or a fourth argument."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"migrate-from-the-previous-return-shape","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrate from the previous return shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Earlier versions returned the pending-items array from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued()"},{"type":"text","value":". It now returns the processed scalar value. Replace "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued().length"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queued.queuer.state().items.length"},{"type":"text","value":" using the default selector, or use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectQueuedSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" when the queue contents are the desired signal value. Custom selectors must include "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":" to access that list."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ordering-items","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ordering items"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic processing uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addItemsTo"},{"type":"text","value":" to choose where new items enter and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getItemsFrom"},{"type":"text","value":" to choose where items leave."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fifo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FIFO"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FIFO processes the oldest item first. This is the default."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  addItemsTo: 'back',\n  getItemsFrom: 'front',\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.addItem(3)\nqueuer.start() // Processes 1, 2, 3.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lifo","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LIFO"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LIFO processes the newest item first."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  addItemsTo: 'back',\n  getItemsFrom: 'back',\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.addItem(3)\nqueuer.start() // Processes 3, 2, 1.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"priority","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Priority"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getPriority"},{"type":"text","value":" to process higher numeric priorities first. Priority ordering takes precedence over front and back retrieval."}]},{"type":"code","value":"type Task = { name: string; priority: number }\n\nconst queuer = injectQueuer<Task>(processTask, {\n  getPriority: (task) => task.priority,\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'low', priority: 1 })\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'high', priority: 3 })\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'medium', priority: 2 })\nqueuer.start() // Processes high, medium, low.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"automatic-and-manual-processing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automatic and manual processing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queues start automatically by default. The first accepted item processes immediately, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wait"},{"type":"text","value":" controls the delay before later items."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  wait: 1000,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"started: false"},{"type":"text","value":" to collect items before processing:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, { started: false })\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.start()\nqueuer.stop()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" cancels the scheduled tick and retains queued items. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start()"},{"type":"text","value":" resumes automatic processing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For manual control:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute()"},{"type":"text","value":" removes and processes the next item immediately."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getNextItem()"},{"type":"text","value":" removes and returns the next item without processing it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"peekNextItem()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the next item without removing it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"peekAllItems()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns a copy of the current queue."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"capacity-and-rejection","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Capacity and rejection"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"},{"type":"text","value":" to bound the number of waiting items. An item added to a full queue is rejected, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addItem()"},{"type":"text","value":" returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReject"},{"type":"text","value":" runs."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  maxSize: 2,\n  started: false,\n  onReject: (item, queuer) => {\n    console.log('Rejected:', item)\n    console.log('Total rejections:', queuer.store.state.rejectionCount)\n  },\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1) // true\nqueuer.addItem(2) // true\nqueuer.addItem(3) // false","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The active synchronous execution is not part of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":" counts items still waiting in the queue."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"expiring-stale-items","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expiring stale items"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expirationDuration"},{"type":"text","value":" to remove items that have waited too long:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  expirationDuration: 5000,\n  onExpire: (item) => {\n    console.log('Expired:', item)\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsExpired"},{"type":"text","value":" for custom logic:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  getIsExpired: (item, addedAt) => Date.now() - addedAt > item.maxAge,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expiration is checked while the automatic processing loop runs. A stopped queue evaluates stale items when processing resumes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flushing-clearing-and-resetting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flushing, clearing, and resetting"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"flush","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Flush"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flush()"},{"type":"text","value":" processes waiting items immediately without the configured delay. Pass a count to process only part of the queue."}]},{"type":"code","value":"queuer.flush() // Process all waiting items.\nqueuer.flush(2) // Process at most two waiting items.","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flushAsBatch()"},{"type":"text","value":" removes all waiting items and passes them to a separate batch function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queuer.flushAsBatch((items) => {\n  saveItems(items)\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"clear","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear()"},{"type":"text","value":" removes all waiting items without processing them. It does not change whether the queue is running."}]},{"type":"code","value":"queuer.clear()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"reset","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reset"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset()"},{"type":"text","value":" restores state to the default running, empty queue. It does not clear an already scheduled timeout. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reset()"},{"type":"text","value":" when scheduled work must be canceled."}]},{"type":"code","value":"queuer.stop()\nqueuer.reset()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuring-and-observing-the-queue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuring and observing the queue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" to update future behavior. Changing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"started"},{"type":"text","value":" through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setOptions()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start()"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"queuer.setOptions({ wait: 250, maxSize: 20 })\nqueuer.start()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"wait"},{"type":"text","value":" option may be a function that receives the queuer instance:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  wait: (queuer) => (queuer.store.state.size > 20 ? 50 : 250),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use callbacks for queue events:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onItemsChange"},{"type":"text","value":": An item was added or removed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExecute"},{"type":"text","value":": An item was processed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onReject"},{"type":"text","value":": An item was rejected."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onExpire"},{"type":"text","value":": An item expired."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"angular-lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter stops automatic processing when its owner is destroyed. Providing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" replaces that default cleanup, so a custom callback must perform every required lifecycle action. When custom cleanup flushes work, remember that user callbacks can run while the component is being destroyed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reactive-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reactive state"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The adapter subscribes only to the state returned by the selector argument. Without a selector, the adapter state is empty. Create the utility in an Angular injection context, usually as a component or service field initializer and select only fields used by the view:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, { wait: 250 }, (state) => ({\n  size: state.size,\n  isRunning: state.isRunning,\n}))\n\nconsole.log(queuer.state().size, queuer.state().isRunning)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option functions and lifecycle callbacks receive the underlying public utility instance. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".store.state"},{"type":"text","value":" reads inside those callbacks in the examples above are supported. Rendering code should read the selected adapter state shown here."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" can restore selected queue state that your app has persisted. If it includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":", they take precedence over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialItems"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState.isRunning"},{"type":"text","value":" likewise takes precedence over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"started"},{"type":"text","value":". Restore only durable fields. Pending timers are not restored."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Commonly useful state includes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":": Items still waiting."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isRunning"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether automatic processing is enabled."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isIdle"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether a running queue is empty."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isFull"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxSize"},{"type":"text","value":" has been reached."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"executionCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Items whose wrapped function returned successfully."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rejectionCount"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expirationCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Items removed without processing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'idle'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'running'"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'stopped'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../reference/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular API reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for adapter signatures and the public core reference for complete option and state types."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"how-queuing-works","text":"How queuing works","level":2},{"id":"when-to-use-queuing","text":"When to use queuing","level":2},{"id":"choose-an-api","text":"Choose an API","level":2},{"id":"angular-example","text":"Angular example","level":2},{"id":"queue-a-source-signal","text":"Queue a source signal","level":2},{"id":"migrate-from-the-previous-return-shape","text":"Migrate from the previous return shape","level":3},{"id":"ordering-items","text":"Ordering items","level":2},{"id":"fifo","text":"FIFO","level":3},{"id":"lifo","text":"LIFO","level":3},{"id":"priority","text":"Priority","level":3},{"id":"automatic-and-manual-processing","text":"Automatic and manual processing","level":2},{"id":"capacity-and-rejection","text":"Capacity and rejection","level":2},{"id":"expiring-stale-items","text":"Expiring stale items","level":2},{"id":"flushing-clearing-and-resetting","text":"Flushing, clearing, and resetting","level":2},{"id":"flush","text":"Flush","level":3},{"id":"clear","text":"Clear","level":3},{"id":"reset","text":"Reset","level":3},{"id":"configuring-and-observing-the-queue","text":"Configuring and observing the queue","level":2},{"id":"angular-lifecycle","text":"Angular lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"reactive-state","text":"Reactive state","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nQueuing stores operations in an ordered buffer and processes them individually. It is the primary Pacer strategy for work that should not be discarded when calls arrive faster than they can run.\n\nQueues are lossless only while they have capacity. A finite `maxSize`, explicit clearing, expiration, or a processing error can still remove or reject work.\n\n## How queuing works\n\n```text\nQueuing (process one item every 2 ticks)\nTimeline: [1 second per tick]\nCalls:        ⬇️  ⬇️  ⬇️     ⬇️  ⬇️     ⬇️  ⬇️  ⬇️\nQueue:       [ABC]   [BC]    [BCDE]    [DE]    [E]    []\nExecuted:     ✅     ✅       ✅        ✅      ✅     ✅\n             [======================================================]\n             ^ Accepted items remain queued until processed\n\n             [Items arrive]    [Process steadily]      [Empty]\n```\n\nThe queue can process automatically with a delay between items, or remain stopped for manual processing.\n\n## When to use queuing\n\nChoose queuing when:\n\n- Every accepted operation should run individually.\n- Processing order matters.\n- Incoming work may temporarily exceed processing capacity.\n- A maximum buffer size should reject excess work explicitly.\n- FIFO, LIFO, or priority ordering is required.\n\nChoose another utility when:\n\n- Only the final call matters. Use [debouncing](./debouncing.md).\n- Intermediate calls may be discarded while work runs steadily. Use [throttling](./throttling.md).\n- Calls should be rejected after a time-window quota. Use [rate limiting](./rate-limiting.md).\n- Items should run together. Use [batching](./batching.md).\n- Tasks return Promises or should run concurrently. Use [async queuing](./async-queuing.md).\n\n## Choose an API\n\n- `injectQueuedSignal` or `injectQueuedValue` for queue-driven signals\n- `injectQueuer` for direct queue lifecycle and ordering control\n\nUse the queued state or value API when queue contents drive the UI. Use the instance API for ordering, capacity, expiration, pause, resume, flush, and manual processing.\n\n## Angular example\n\n```ts\nimport { injectQueuedSignal } from '@tanstack/angular-pacer'\n\nexport class JobQueueComponent {\n  readonly queued = injectQueuedSignal(processJob, { wait: 500 }, (state) => ({\n    items: state.items,\n    isRunning: state.isRunning,\n  }))\n\n  add() {\n    this.queued.addItem(nextJob())\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe focused snippets later in this guide use `injectQueuer` and assume they run inside an Angular injection context.\n\nPass `initialItems` when work is already available at creation time. The queue applies its normal insertion and capacity rules, and automatic processing can begin immediately unless `started: false` is set.\n\n## Queue a source signal\n\n`injectQueuedValue` returns a `QueuedValueSignal`: `queued()` reads the most recently processed value, `queued.addItem(value)` enqueues a value, and `queued.queuer` exposes the queue controls. Its default selector exposes pending items at `queued.queuer.state().items`.\n\n```ts\nreadonly source = input.required<string>()\nreadonly queued = injectQueuedValue(this.source, { wait: 500 })\n```\n\nConstruction does not read the source. Angular's effect reads it after inputs are bound and enqueues the latest value. Each later effect run enqueues the latest observed source value. Several source writes before an effect runs are coalesced; use `queued.addItem` for every value that must enter the queue individually.\n\nBefore processing begins, `queued()` reads the initial source value. Reading it before a required input is bound throws Angular's required-input error. Supply an explicit initial value if the output must be readable earlier:\n\n```ts\nconst text = injectQueuedValue(source, '')\nconst object = injectQueuedValue(objectSource, { label: 'Loading' }, {})\nconst callback = injectQueuedValue(callbackSource, () => 'Loading', {})\n```\n\nTwo-argument primitive initial values, including `0`, `false`, `''`, and `null`, are supported. Object and function initial values require a third options object, such as `{}`. A function in the options position is an options factory.\n\nPass a fourth selector argument, which can be `undefined`, when an explicit initial value uses factory or undefined options:\n\n```ts\nconst queued = injectQueuedValue(source, '', () => ({ wait: wait() }), undefined)\nconst initialObject = injectQueuedValue(objectSource, { label: 'Loading' }, undefined, undefined)\n```\n\n`injectQueuedValue(source, options, undefined)` keeps the options-only meaning. An explicit `undefined` initial value requires an options object or a fourth argument.\n\n### Migrate from the previous return shape\n\nEarlier versions returned the pending-items array from `queued()`. It now returns the processed scalar value. Replace `queued().length` with `queued.queuer.state().items.length` using the default selector, or use `injectQueuedSignal` when the queue contents are the desired signal value. Custom selectors must include `items` to access that list.\n\n## Ordering items\n\nAutomatic processing uses `addItemsTo` to choose where new items enter and `getItemsFrom` to choose where items leave.\n\n### FIFO\n\nFIFO processes the oldest item first. This is the default.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  addItemsTo: 'back',\n  getItemsFrom: 'front',\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.addItem(3)\nqueuer.start() // Processes 1, 2, 3.\n```\n\n### LIFO\n\nLIFO processes the newest item first.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  addItemsTo: 'back',\n  getItemsFrom: 'back',\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.addItem(3)\nqueuer.start() // Processes 3, 2, 1.\n```\n\n### Priority\n\nProvide `getPriority` to process higher numeric priorities first. Priority ordering takes precedence over front and back retrieval.\n\n```ts\ntype Task = { name: string; priority: number }\n\nconst queuer = injectQueuer<Task>(processTask, {\n  getPriority: (task) => task.priority,\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'low', priority: 1 })\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'high', priority: 3 })\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'medium', priority: 2 })\nqueuer.start() // Processes high, medium, low.\n```\n\n## Automatic and manual processing\n\nQueues start automatically by default. The first accepted item processes immediately, then `wait` controls the delay before later items.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  wait: 1000,\n})\n```\n\nSet `started: false` to collect items before processing:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, { started: false })\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.start()\nqueuer.stop()\n```\n\n`stop()` cancels the scheduled tick and retains queued items. `start()` resumes automatic processing.\n\nFor manual control:\n\n- `execute()` removes and processes the next item immediately.\n- `getNextItem()` removes and returns the next item without processing it.\n- `peekNextItem()` returns the next item without removing it.\n- `peekAllItems()` returns a copy of the current queue.\n\n## Capacity and rejection\n\nSet `maxSize` to bound the number of waiting items. An item added to a full queue is rejected, `addItem()` returns `false`, and `onReject` runs.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  maxSize: 2,\n  started: false,\n  onReject: (item, queuer) => {\n    console.log('Rejected:', item)\n    console.log('Total rejections:', queuer.store.state.rejectionCount)\n  },\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1) // true\nqueuer.addItem(2) // true\nqueuer.addItem(3) // false\n```\n\nThe active synchronous execution is not part of `size`; `size` counts items still waiting in the queue.\n\n## Expiring stale items\n\nUse `expirationDuration` to remove items that have waited too long:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  expirationDuration: 5000,\n  onExpire: (item) => {\n    console.log('Expired:', item)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUse `getIsExpired` for custom logic:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  getIsExpired: (item, addedAt) => Date.now() - addedAt > item.maxAge,\n})\n```\n\nExpiration is checked while the automatic processing loop runs. A stopped queue evaluates stale items when processing resumes.\n\n## Flushing, clearing, and resetting\n\n### Flush\n\n`flush()` processes waiting items immediately without the configured delay. Pass a count to process only part of the queue.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.flush() // Process all waiting items.\nqueuer.flush(2) // Process at most two waiting items.\n```\n\n`flushAsBatch()` removes all waiting items and passes them to a separate batch function:\n\n```ts\nqueuer.flushAsBatch((items) => {\n  saveItems(items)\n})\n```\n\n### Clear\n\n`clear()` removes all waiting items without processing them. It does not change whether the queue is running.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.clear()\n```\n\n### Reset\n\n`reset()` restores state to the default running, empty queue. It does not clear an already scheduled timeout. Call `stop()` before `reset()` when scheduled work must be canceled.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.stop()\nqueuer.reset()\n```\n\n## Configuring and observing the queue\n\nUse `setOptions()` to update future behavior. Changing `started` through `setOptions()` does not call `start()` or `stop()`.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.setOptions({ wait: 250, maxSize: 20 })\nqueuer.start()\n```\n\nThe `wait` option may be a function that receives the queuer instance:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  wait: (queuer) => (queuer.store.state.size > 20 ? 50 : 250),\n})\n```\n\nUse callbacks for queue events:\n\n- `onItemsChange`: An item was added or removed.\n- `onExecute`: An item was processed.\n- `onReject`: An item was rejected.\n- `onExpire`: An item expired.\n\n## Angular lifecycle\n\nThe adapter stops automatic processing when its owner is destroyed. Providing `onUnmount` replaces that default cleanup, so a custom callback must perform every required lifecycle action. When custom cleanup flushes work, remember that user callbacks can run while the component is being destroyed.\n\n## Reactive state\n\nThe adapter subscribes only to the state returned by the selector argument. Without a selector, the adapter state is empty. Create the utility in an Angular injection context, usually as a component or service field initializer and select only fields used by the view:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, { wait: 250 }, (state) => ({\n  size: state.size,\n  isRunning: state.isRunning,\n}))\n\nconsole.log(queuer.state().size, queuer.state().isRunning)\n```\n\nOption functions and lifecycle callbacks receive the underlying public utility instance. The `.store.state` reads inside those callbacks in the examples above are supported. Rendering code should read the selected adapter state shown here.\n\n`initialState` can restore selected queue state that your app has persisted. If it includes `items`, they take precedence over `initialItems`; `initialState.isRunning` likewise takes precedence over `started`. Restore only durable fields. Pending timers are not restored.\n\nCommonly useful state includes:\n\n- `items` and `size`: Items still waiting.\n- `isRunning`: Whether automatic processing is enabled.\n- `isIdle`: Whether a running queue is empty.\n- `isFull`: Whether `maxSize` has been reached.\n- `executionCount`: Items whose wrapped function returned successfully.\n- `rejectionCount` and `expirationCount`: Items removed without processing.\n- `status`: `'idle'`, `'running'`, or `'stopped'`.\n\nSee the [Angular API reference](../reference/index.md) for adapter signatures and the public core reference for complete option and state types.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Angular Queuing Guide\nid: queuing\n---\n\nQueuing stores operations in an ordered buffer and processes them individually. It is the primary Pacer strategy for work that should not be discarded when calls arrive faster than they can run.\n\nQueues are lossless only while they have capacity. A finite `maxSize`, explicit clearing, expiration, or a processing error can still remove or reject work.\n\n## How queuing works\n\n```text\nQueuing (process one item every 2 ticks)\nTimeline: [1 second per tick]\nCalls:        ⬇️  ⬇️  ⬇️     ⬇️  ⬇️     ⬇️  ⬇️  ⬇️\nQueue:       [ABC]   [BC]    [BCDE]    [DE]    [E]    []\nExecuted:     ✅     ✅       ✅        ✅      ✅     ✅\n             [======================================================]\n             ^ Accepted items remain queued until processed\n\n             [Items arrive]    [Process steadily]      [Empty]\n```\n\nThe queue can process automatically with a delay between items, or remain stopped for manual processing.\n\n## When to use queuing\n\nChoose queuing when:\n\n- Every accepted operation should run individually.\n- Processing order matters.\n- Incoming work may temporarily exceed processing capacity.\n- A maximum buffer size should reject excess work explicitly.\n- FIFO, LIFO, or priority ordering is required.\n\nChoose another utility when:\n\n- Only the final call matters. Use [debouncing](./debouncing.md).\n- Intermediate calls may be discarded while work runs steadily. Use [throttling](./throttling.md).\n- Calls should be rejected after a time-window quota. Use [rate limiting](./rate-limiting.md).\n- Items should run together. Use [batching](./batching.md).\n- Tasks return Promises or should run concurrently. Use [async queuing](./async-queuing.md).\n\n## Choose an API\n\n- `injectQueuedSignal` or `injectQueuedValue` for queue-driven signals\n- `injectQueuer` for direct queue lifecycle and ordering control\n\nUse the queued state or value API when queue contents drive the UI. Use the instance API for ordering, capacity, expiration, pause, resume, flush, and manual processing.\n\n## Angular example\n\n```ts\nimport { injectQueuedSignal } from '@tanstack/angular-pacer'\n\nexport class JobQueueComponent {\n  readonly queued = injectQueuedSignal(processJob, { wait: 500 }, (state) => ({\n    items: state.items,\n    isRunning: state.isRunning,\n  }))\n\n  add() {\n    this.queued.addItem(nextJob())\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe focused snippets later in this guide use `injectQueuer` and assume they run inside an Angular injection context.\n\nPass `initialItems` when work is already available at creation time. The queue applies its normal insertion and capacity rules, and automatic processing can begin immediately unless `started: false` is set.\n\n## Queue a source signal\n\n`injectQueuedValue` returns a `QueuedValueSignal`: `queued()` reads the most recently processed value, `queued.addItem(value)` enqueues a value, and `queued.queuer` exposes the queue controls. Its default selector exposes pending items at `queued.queuer.state().items`.\n\n```ts\nreadonly source = input.required<string>()\nreadonly queued = injectQueuedValue(this.source, { wait: 500 })\n```\n\nConstruction does not read the source. Angular's effect reads it after inputs are bound and enqueues the latest value. Each later effect run enqueues the latest observed source value. Several source writes before an effect runs are coalesced; use `queued.addItem` for every value that must enter the queue individually.\n\nBefore processing begins, `queued()` reads the initial source value. Reading it before a required input is bound throws Angular's required-input error. Supply an explicit initial value if the output must be readable earlier:\n\n```ts\nconst text = injectQueuedValue(source, '')\nconst object = injectQueuedValue(objectSource, { label: 'Loading' }, {})\nconst callback = injectQueuedValue(callbackSource, () => 'Loading', {})\n```\n\nTwo-argument primitive initial values, including `0`, `false`, `''`, and `null`, are supported. Object and function initial values require a third options object, such as `{}`. A function in the options position is an options factory.\n\nPass a fourth selector argument, which can be `undefined`, when an explicit initial value uses factory or undefined options:\n\n```ts\nconst queued = injectQueuedValue(source, '', () => ({ wait: wait() }), undefined)\nconst initialObject = injectQueuedValue(objectSource, { label: 'Loading' }, undefined, undefined)\n```\n\n`injectQueuedValue(source, options, undefined)` keeps the options-only meaning. An explicit `undefined` initial value requires an options object or a fourth argument.\n\n### Migrate from the previous return shape\n\nEarlier versions returned the pending-items array from `queued()`. It now returns the processed scalar value. Replace `queued().length` with `queued.queuer.state().items.length` using the default selector, or use `injectQueuedSignal` when the queue contents are the desired signal value. Custom selectors must include `items` to access that list.\n\n## Ordering items\n\nAutomatic processing uses `addItemsTo` to choose where new items enter and `getItemsFrom` to choose where items leave.\n\n### FIFO\n\nFIFO processes the oldest item first. This is the default.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  addItemsTo: 'back',\n  getItemsFrom: 'front',\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.addItem(3)\nqueuer.start() // Processes 1, 2, 3.\n```\n\n### LIFO\n\nLIFO processes the newest item first.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  addItemsTo: 'back',\n  getItemsFrom: 'back',\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.addItem(3)\nqueuer.start() // Processes 3, 2, 1.\n```\n\n### Priority\n\nProvide `getPriority` to process higher numeric priorities first. Priority ordering takes precedence over front and back retrieval.\n\n```ts\ntype Task = { name: string; priority: number }\n\nconst queuer = injectQueuer<Task>(processTask, {\n  getPriority: (task) => task.priority,\n  started: false,\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'low', priority: 1 })\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'high', priority: 3 })\nqueuer.addItem({ name: 'medium', priority: 2 })\nqueuer.start() // Processes high, medium, low.\n```\n\n## Automatic and manual processing\n\nQueues start automatically by default. The first accepted item processes immediately, then `wait` controls the delay before later items.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  wait: 1000,\n})\n```\n\nSet `started: false` to collect items before processing:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, { started: false })\n\nqueuer.addItem(1)\nqueuer.addItem(2)\nqueuer.start()\nqueuer.stop()\n```\n\n`stop()` cancels the scheduled tick and retains queued items. `start()` resumes automatic processing.\n\nFor manual control:\n\n- `execute()` removes and processes the next item immediately.\n- `getNextItem()` removes and returns the next item without processing it.\n- `peekNextItem()` returns the next item without removing it.\n- `peekAllItems()` returns a copy of the current queue.\n\n## Capacity and rejection\n\nSet `maxSize` to bound the number of waiting items. An item added to a full queue is rejected, `addItem()` returns `false`, and `onReject` runs.\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  maxSize: 2,\n  started: false,\n  onReject: (item, queuer) => {\n    console.log('Rejected:', item)\n    console.log('Total rejections:', queuer.store.state.rejectionCount)\n  },\n})\n\nqueuer.addItem(1) // true\nqueuer.addItem(2) // true\nqueuer.addItem(3) // false\n```\n\nThe active synchronous execution is not part of `size`; `size` counts items still waiting in the queue.\n\n## Expiring stale items\n\nUse `expirationDuration` to remove items that have waited too long:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  expirationDuration: 5000,\n  onExpire: (item) => {\n    console.log('Expired:', item)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUse `getIsExpired` for custom logic:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  getIsExpired: (item, addedAt) => Date.now() - addedAt > item.maxAge,\n})\n```\n\nExpiration is checked while the automatic processing loop runs. A stopped queue evaluates stale items when processing resumes.\n\n## Flushing, clearing, and resetting\n\n### Flush\n\n`flush()` processes waiting items immediately without the configured delay. Pass a count to process only part of the queue.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.flush() // Process all waiting items.\nqueuer.flush(2) // Process at most two waiting items.\n```\n\n`flushAsBatch()` removes all waiting items and passes them to a separate batch function:\n\n```ts\nqueuer.flushAsBatch((items) => {\n  saveItems(items)\n})\n```\n\n### Clear\n\n`clear()` removes all waiting items without processing them. It does not change whether the queue is running.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.clear()\n```\n\n### Reset\n\n`reset()` restores state to the default running, empty queue. It does not clear an already scheduled timeout. Call `stop()` before `reset()` when scheduled work must be canceled.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.stop()\nqueuer.reset()\n```\n\n## Configuring and observing the queue\n\nUse `setOptions()` to update future behavior. Changing `started` through `setOptions()` does not call `start()` or `stop()`.\n\n```ts\nqueuer.setOptions({ wait: 250, maxSize: 20 })\nqueuer.start()\n```\n\nThe `wait` option may be a function that receives the queuer instance:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, {\n  wait: (queuer) => (queuer.store.state.size > 20 ? 50 : 250),\n})\n```\n\nUse callbacks for queue events:\n\n- `onItemsChange`: An item was added or removed.\n- `onExecute`: An item was processed.\n- `onReject`: An item was rejected.\n- `onExpire`: An item expired.\n\n## Angular lifecycle\n\nThe adapter stops automatic processing when its owner is destroyed. Providing `onUnmount` replaces that default cleanup, so a custom callback must perform every required lifecycle action. When custom cleanup flushes work, remember that user callbacks can run while the component is being destroyed.\n\n## Reactive state\n\nThe adapter subscribes only to the state returned by the selector argument. Without a selector, the adapter state is empty. Create the utility in an Angular injection context, usually as a component or service field initializer and select only fields used by the view:\n\n```ts\nconst queuer = injectQueuer(processItem, { wait: 250 }, (state) => ({\n  size: state.size,\n  isRunning: state.isRunning,\n}))\n\nconsole.log(queuer.state().size, queuer.state().isRunning)\n```\n\nOption functions and lifecycle callbacks receive the underlying public utility instance. The `.store.state` reads inside those callbacks in the examples above are supported. Rendering code should read the selected adapter state shown here.\n\n`initialState` can restore selected queue state that your app has persisted. If it includes `items`, they take precedence over `initialItems`; `initialState.isRunning` likewise takes precedence over `started`. Restore only durable fields. Pending timers are not restored.\n\nCommonly useful state includes:\n\n- `items` and `size`: Items still waiting.\n- `isRunning`: Whether automatic processing is enabled.\n- `isIdle`: Whether a running queue is empty.\n- `isFull`: Whether `maxSize` has been reached.\n- `executionCount`: Items whose wrapped function returned successfully.\n- `rejectionCount` and `expirationCount`: Items removed without processing.\n- `status`: `'idle'`, `'running'`, or `'stopped'`.\n\nSee the [Angular API reference](../reference/index.md) for adapter signatures and the public core reference for complete option and state types.\n"}
